---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---
<PolicyLayout title="Privacy Notice">
  <p><em>Last updated: 1 September 2026</em></p>

  <p>This privacy notice explains how Science Works Limited uses your personal information. It tells you what we collect, why, and what rights you have.</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>Science Works Limited is a company limited by guarantee registered in England and Wales, company number 17034971. Our registered office is 167–169 Great Portland Street, London, W1W 5PF.</p>
  <p>Science Works Limited is the controller. Contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@science.works">contact@science.works</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

  <h3>When you contact us</h3>
  <p>If you email us or use a contact form on our website, we collect your name, email address and the contents of your message. We use this information to reply to you and manage our relationship with you.</p>
  <p>Our legal basis is legitimate interests: responding to people who contact us and keeping appropriate records of our communications.</p>
  <p>We keep this information for as long as we need to deal with your enquiry and any necessary follow-up, and delete it when it is no longer needed.</p>

  <h3>When you sign up for updates</h3>
  <p>If you sign up to hear from us, we collect your email address and your mailing-list preferences. We use this information to send you updates about our work.</p>
  <p>Our legal basis is consent: you actively chose to sign up. You can withdraw your consent at any time by using the unsubscribe link in our emails.</p>
  <p>Brevo stores our mailing-list information in the European Union under UK adequacy arrangements.</p>
  <p>We keep your email address for as long as you are subscribed. If you unsubscribe, we delete it from our active mailing list within 10 working days, subject to any minimal suppression record needed to ensure that we do not contact you again.</p>

  <h3>When you complete a Science Works survey</h3>
  <p>We may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name and email address;</li>
    <li>your organisation and role, if you choose to provide them;</li>
    <li>your answers, ratings and free-text comments;</li>
    <li>whether you have separately chosen to join our mailing list;</li>
    <li>the date and time at which a response was created or updated; and</li>
    <li>technical information needed to save your answers and allow you to return to them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use this information to understand views about the research system, analyse patterns and differences in responses, inform Science Works' research and priorities, and improve our projects and events.</p>
  <p>Our legal basis for ordinary personal information is legitimate interests: conducting and improving our research and activities. Joining our mailing list is separate and is based on consent.</p>
  <p>We keep identifiable survey responses for 24 months.</p>

  <h3>When you attend a Science Works event or retreat</h3>
  <p>We may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, contact details, organisation and role;</li>
    <li>attendance, accommodation, accessibility, catering or dietary information needed to run the event;</li>
    <li>a biography and profile photograph;</li>
    <li>answers to pre-event and post-event surveys;</li>
    <li>feedback, ratings and free-text comments;</li>
    <li>information about people or organisations you recommend to us;</li>
    <li>notes, recordings, photographs, presentations or other files that you choose to upload; and</li>
    <li>website access and sign-in records.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use this information to organise and administer the event, provide attendees with relevant information, enable appropriate introductions, evaluate and improve the event, plan follow-up work and keep the attendee-only website secure.</p>
  <p>We rely on legitimate interests to administer, evaluate and secure events and to display attendee profiles on the restricted retreat website, helping participants understand who is involved and make connections. We display event photographs on the restricted attendee website with your consent.</p>
  <p>We delete information collected only to run the event, such as accommodation, catering and dietary information, 30 days after the event. We keep event registration and access records, and identifiable survey and feedback responses, for 24 months. We keep attendee profiles and photographs on the retreat website for 12 months.</p>

  <h3>Files uploaded through Google Forms</h3>
  <p>If you upload notes, recordings, photographs or other files through our Google Form, Google records the name, email address and profile photograph associated with your Google Account. The form may also ask for your name.</p>
  <p>The uploaded files are copied to storage controlled by Science Works. This means they are shared outside the Google Workspace organisation from which you upload them. We use them to document, evaluate and follow up the event.</p>
  <p>We use Google Forms and Google Drive to collect and store these files.</p>
  <p><strong>Uploaded files are not shared with Wellcome or with any other event partner, and no partner has access to them.</strong></p>

  <h3>Information about other people</h3>
  <p>We may receive information about you from someone completing a survey or event form. We use it to consider you as a possible speaker, attendee, collaborator or contact. Our legal basis is legitimate interests: identifying such people.</p>

  <h2>Who we share your information with</h2>
  <p>We may share personal information with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>our mailing-list provider;</li>
    <li>Google, through Google Workspace, Google Forms and Google Drive;</li>
    <li>our website and database hosting providers;</li>
    <li>an event partner such as Wellcome, where necessary for an event and as explained above;</li>
    <li>professional advisers or authorities where this is necessary to comply with the law, protect our rights or deal with a legal claim.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>Some suppliers process personal information outside the UK, including in the United States. Where UK adequacy regulations apply, including the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, we rely on them. Otherwise, we use the UK International Data Transfer Addendum to the EU standard contractual clauses. You can ask for a copy of the relevant safeguards by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@science.works">contact@science.works</a>.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep your information</h2>
  <p>The specific periods applying to mailing-list, survey and event information are described above. We review personal information periodically and delete or anonymise it when it is no longer needed, subject to any legal, accounting or safeguarding requirement to retain it for longer.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on the circumstances, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct information that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your personal information;</li>
    <li>ask us to restrict or stop using your personal information;</li>
    <li>ask for personal information you provided to us in a portable format; and</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time where we rely on consent, without affecting our earlier use of your information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where we rely on legitimate interests, you have the right to object to our use of your personal information.</p>
  <p>To make a request, email <a href="mailto:contact@science.works">contact@science.works</a>.</p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>You have the right to complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
